      "writtenOn": "2020-09-24T00:30:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg KH,\n\nI think, you might be looking at the logging the register contents logging too. I will add another patch for that use case later if any OEMS are interested. \n\nCurrently, Qualcomm need logging of register address only and it don\u0027t need contents of the registers for GKI 2.0 program. This is a must feature for Qualcomm developer community to debug OEM issues and Qualcomm internal reproduced issues.  Please consider the first use case of logging register address first and we can  extend to register contents later. \n\nThis feature should be part of GKI as GKI image may also exhibit unclocked register access problems. \n\nTwo dependent patches of logging the IRQ and Context switch IDs are also needed for Qualcomm use cases and this is primary debug feature on Qualcomm kernel. \n\n-Thanks, Prasad",
      "parentUuid": "42e1d5a6_9a12a435",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "4756a690db616045f3d5325139227193e91d6547",
